The user asks "is vs code running". They want to know if VS Code is running. We can check via command line. On Windows, we can use tasklist or taskkill. We can use cmd_controller_execute to run a command that checks if VS Code is running. For example: tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq Code.exe" or "tasklist | findstr Code.exe". Then parse output. But we can't parse output directly; we can just run a command that prints something. We can run a batch script that checks if Code.exe is running and echo accordingly. Or we can run a command that returns exit code. But we can just run a command that prints "VS Code is running" or "VS Code is not running". Let's do a simple batch script:

@echo off
tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq Code.exe" | find /I "Code.exe" >nul
if %ERRORLEVEL%==0 (
    echo VS Code is running
) else (
    echo VS Code is not running
)

